# Stradivarius violin — buyable / purchasable findings (web snapshot)

**Generated:** 2026-05-11 (UTC)  
**Scope:** This file records instruments and listings discovered via public web search on that date. It is **not** an exhaustive crawl of the entire internet; URLs and availability change daily. Verify price, authenticity, and stock before paying.

**Important distinction:** Almost all affordable listings are **copies or instruments bearing a facsimile “Antonius Stradivarius” label** (a common German/Czech trade practice), **not** violins made by Antonio Stradivari (1644–1737). Genuine Strads are sold almost exclusively through major auction houses, elite dealers, or private treaty; expect seven- to eight-figure prices and independent certification.

---

## A. Genuine Antonio Stradivari violins (auction / private treaty channels)

### A1. Kodner Galleries — “The McKay,” Antonio Stradivari, Cremona, c. 1737

- **Channel:** Kodner Auctions catalog (“Stradivarius Violin, Estate Jewelry & Decoration,” 2025-10-08). Lot page still published as of 2026-05-11 fetch; **confirm with gallery whether unsold / available for post-auction sale.**
- **Estimate (catalog):** USD 2,000,000 – 9,000,000  
- **Notes:** Hill certificate (reissued 2015), dendrochronology, extensive provenance (Gordon McKay, BSO/NYP players). **Online bidding was not available** for this lot; registration was through Kodner directly, deposit required.
- **Lot URL:** https://www.kodner.com/auctions/2025/10/08/stradivarius-violin-estate-jewelry-decoration/81  
- **Auction hub:** https://www.kodner.com/auctions/2025/10/08/stradivarius-violin-estate-jewelry-decoration/  
- **Contact:** help@kodner.com — +1 954-925-2550 (per catalog)

